    "version": 1,
    "task": "Record all decisions on a review at once: reviews --decide-template prints a skeleton, --decide-file records it in one validated write per commit",
    "summary": "One call per finding was slow for an arbiter with a dozen findings. Now a template lists each ref, the arbiter fills outcomes, and the file is validated entirely before one compare-and-swap write per commit, so a bad row records nothing. The input is untrusted-shaped (size, depth, keys), so it is bounded and read field by field.",
    "groups": [
      {
        "id": "batch-parse",
        "intent": "Read a bounded decisions file, validate it, and build the template",
        "necessity": "required",
        "serves": "task",
        "removal_impact": "No batch input could be read safely, and the template would not exist",
        "impact": "contract",
        "impact_reason": "defines the accepted file shapes and limits (500 entries, 1 MiB)",
        "hunks": [
          "h4"
        ],
        "notes": "Size and entry count are capped; nesting depth is not bounded: JSON.parse recursion errors are caught and reported. Template text is cut at 80 code points. A non-blocking stdin is waited for. Template rows write a bare ref as \"N: text\" (so refOf recognises it) and a repeated finding is refused."
      },
      {
        "id": "batch-command",
        "intent": "Wire --decide-template and --decide-file into reviews",
        "necessity": "required",
        "serves": "task",
        "removal_impact": "The batch flags would not exist",
        "impact": "contract",
        "impact_reason": "new CLI flags and a stdout summary line; writes decision records",
        "hunks": [
          "h5",
          "h6",
          "h7",
          "h8",
          "h9"
        ],
        "notes": "Flag conflicts, validate first, one addReviews per commit, warn on unknown refs, summary line. reportOf and warnUnknownRef are shared by the template, file and single paths; the single call reuses checkLength."
      },
      {
        "id": "finding-texts",
